delta-change "source-maps-layout"
message "SourceMapLayout: AST source maps and graph-defined layout tokens"
author "ai"
doc "guide" """
  |# SourceMapLayout: semantic source maps and layout events
  |
  |SourceMapLayout is the eighth post-constitution grammar product layer. It is derived from the frozen SourceProvenance product graph by a canonical DeltaTrellis change. It is not F12 and does not alter the frozen F0–F11 bootstrap constitution.
  |
  |## Identities
  |
  |- SourceMapLayout delta: `d7f8d8ccfb49a1d0353da18aaf419d4a456824298ef713268823fe4e84cc2016`
  |- SourceMapLayout root: `f19d5ea4d3531c6f3ccea5877cc4199a15908966722a4ef38ce603ae5151aba4`
  |- Graph size: 488 nodes, 662 edges, 488 entities
  |
  |## Purpose
  |
  |SourceProvenance established a lossless lexical source envelope with UTF-8 byte spans and preserved trivia. SourceMapLayout builds two independent semantic views over that envelope:
  |
  |1. AST source maps: each semantic tree node receives a half-open UTF-8 byte envelope derived from the actual source tokens that produced it.
  |2. Layout events: indentation-sensitive source produces virtual `NEWLINE`, `INDENT`, and `DEDENT` events according to graph-resident policy.
  |
  |Neither feature destroys source text. `SourceDocument.renderLossless` remains byte-for-byte equal to the original source.
  |
  |## AST source maps
  |
  |The graph defines `source.map.bool0.policy` and connects it to `grammar.bool0` with role `grammar.source-map`. The policy requires:
  |
  |- UTF-8 byte coordinates,
  |- token-envelope node spans,
  |- field/index paths,
  |- fail-closed behavior.
  |
  |The host derives maps by replaying the graph grammar over source-token slices and comparing semantic trees. It does not infer spans from normalized pretty-print text. Consequently lexical normalization such as `0007 -> 7` preserves the original `[0,4)` source span.
  |
  |Paths are structural:
  |
  |- `$` for the root,
  |- `$.left` for a scalar field,
  |- `$.value` for a present optional field,
  |- `$.items[0]` for repeated captures.
  |
  |## Layout
  |
  |The graph defines `layout.bool0.policy` and connects it to `grammar.bool0` with role `grammar.layout`. The initial policy is:
  |
  |- mode: `offside`,
  |- indentation: spaces,
  |- indent unit: 2,
  |- tabs: reject,
  |- blank lines: ignore,
  |- comment-only lines: ignore,
  |- root indentation: 0,
  |- EOF dedent: required,
  |- failure: fail closed.
  |
  |The policy refers to first-class `layout.token` entities for `NEWLINE`, `INDENT`, and `DEDENT`.
  |
  |Layout events are virtual. Whitespace and comments remain in SourceProvenance source provenance, so layout interpretation and exact source reconstruction coexist.
  |
  |## Laws
  |
  |SourceMapLayout preserves the earlier semantic and source laws and adds:
  |
  |```text
  |parseWithSource(source).tree == parse(source)
  |parseWithSource(source).document.renderLossless == source
  |sourceMap(root).span == token envelope of the semantic root
  |layoutSource(source).source.renderLossless == source
  |layout events are deterministic under a fixed graph policy
  |```
  |
  |## Evolution
  |
  |`DeltaBool0` admits `source.map-policy` and `layout.policy` as first-class change targets. Changing the indentation unit therefore changes layout behavior without modifying Scala code. Unsupported policies, tab indentation, non-multiple indentation, and unmatched dedents fail closed.
  |
  """
test "canonical delta contract"
  assert "canonical"
  assert "valid"
  assert "source-roundtrip"
  assert "dependency" "source-provenance"
  assert "introduces" "grammar.component.source-map" "grammar.component"
